# Keep the build context small. Without this, `docker build .` uploads
# everything in the working tree to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs — and this repository's `data/` holds TPC-H datasets up to 100 GB, plus
# `target/` after a release build. The result is a build that appears to hang
# for minutes on "sending build context" and can fill the daemon's disk.
#
# Data is MOUNTED at runtime (see k8s/statefulset.yaml), never baked in.

data/
target/
.git/
.github/
logs/
.scratch/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Not needed to build the binary. `benches/` IS needed: Cargo.toml declares a
# [[bench]] target and Cargo refuses to load a manifest whose target file is
# missing, even for `cargo build --bin`.
tests/
docs/
k8s/
scripts/
.claude/
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
kind-cluster.yaml
